`@project` and HTML builder slots are implemented. General `$entry` and runtime `io.set_title` remain queued. See @../progress (Progress).

### Using `@project`

Bind `@project` to read predefined project fields:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    @project version

    footer #= [: v[version]]
]

`@project` is never implicitly injected.

### HTML metadata

Direct const inserts on an active root set document metadata:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    #[$in title:About]
    #[$in stylesheets:[@styles/site.css]]
    #[: <main>About this site</main>]
]

HTML also accepts `description`, `lang`, `favicon`, `body_style` and `head`.
Repeated scalar contributions concatenate. A supplied empty value differs from
an absent slot. An absent title uses the route and then the project name with
the configured prefix and postfix; absent description emits nothing and the
other values use builder defaults. The builder escapes title text and attribute
values. Each stylesheet insert needs one tracked CSS resource. The builder keeps
the first contribution for each resource origin and renders its URL relative to
the output page.

`head` inserts raw HTML after built-in head content. Identical complete head
contributions render once. Old `page_*` constants have no implicit metadata
effect. JavaScript and HTML-Wasm documents use the same slot plan.

A metadata-only root still produces a page because a direct const contribution
counts as root activity. Runtime top-level templates contribute only to the
body; runtime named builder slots are unsettled and are not supported. General
`$entry` root purpose and runtime title mutation remain separate future
features. The earlier `$page` proposal is superseded and is not current syntax.

### Concepts related to entry basics

- For build configuration values see @#build-inputs (Build configuration values).
